{"authored" [{"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0+4}-2}{0}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+4}-2)(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x+4-4}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-1)}{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x-\\sqrt{x})(2x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{4{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(4x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{\\cancel{(4x-1)}(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x\\cancel{(4x-1)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{2x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0c9e17a10adfc0320287732d151ca51250173d99882edfdc43daf2517459383" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/state.json" "file_sha256" "5b0dc91f6204bab941929f599373d23f9fbcf83b5bcdc822ef56d97b4fdf04e2" "basis" 1272 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037545/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0+4}-2}{0}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+4}-2)(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x+4-4}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6be43f8ab42b257745d4f78134c4c44ef2e1d195c07c6639125c89e280f2c5ae"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-4463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}-1}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x-7}-1}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2x-7}-1)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{2x-7})}^{2}-{1}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-7-1}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2x-8}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2(x-4)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{2x-7}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2(4)-7}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6be43f8ab42b257745d4f78134c4c44ef2e1d195c07c6639125c89e280f2c5ae"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-107060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & =\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5(5)}}{5-5}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{5x}}{5-x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{(5-\\sqrt{5x})(5+\\sqrt{5x})}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{{5}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5x})}^{2}}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{25-5x}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5(5-x)}{(5-x)(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5\\cancel{(5-x)}}{\\cancel{(5-x)}(5+\\sqrt{5x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 5}\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{5(5)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5+\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6be43f8ab42b257745d4f78134c4c44ef2e1d195c07c6639125c89e280f2c5ae"} {"question" "q-338477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-1)}{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x-\\sqrt{x})(2x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{4{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(4x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{\\cancel{(4x-1)}(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x\\cancel{(4x-1)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{2x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6be43f8ab42b257745d4f78134c4c44ef2e1d195c07c6639125c89e280f2c5ae"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338496" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=3$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & =\\frac{3-3}{3(3)-\\sqrt{27(3)}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{3x-\\sqrt{27x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x-\\sqrt{27x})(3x+\\sqrt{27x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{(3x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{27x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9{x}^{2}-27x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x(x-3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(3x+\\sqrt{27x})}{9x\\cancel{(x-3)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{27x}}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3)+\\sqrt{27(3)}}{9(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+9}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6be43f8ab42b257745d4f78134c4c44ef2e1d195c07c6639125c89e280f2c5ae"} {"question" "q-338504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040785/state.json" "file_sha256" "181ce8f9e92d5b6d0302e7b493edf0a51cf9385bef022cde8f5866c1fd381dec"} {"question" "q-338504" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1404078